Leveraging Retrieval-Augmented Language Models for Early Diagnosis in Resource-Constrained Healthcare
(RAG + RAE Framework for Data Augmentation and Clinical Diagnosis)

This repository provides a complete, reproducible pipeline for retrieval-augmented data generation (RAG) and retrieval-aware evaluation (RAE) to support early diagnosis when only small datasets are available.
The workflow includes:

1) RAG-based data augmentation (LLM-only and LLM+RAG variants)
2) Diagnostic modeling with RAE, using original and augmented datasets
3) Evaluation of performance with and without fine-tuning

What This Repository Contains?
The main script (or notebook) included in this repo allow you to run the full pipeline:
1. RAG-Based Augmentation (This module generates additional synthetic clinical samples based on your small dataset using:
1.1 LLM-Based Augmentation
1.2 LLM + RAG Augmentation (retrieves context-relevant samples before generation)
1.3 Diagnosis with RAE (Retrieval-Aware Evaluation)
The file that contains the related code can ba found here: 

From where to download the case-study dataset (appendicitis)?
 * Download Dataset Here: https://physionet.org/content/mimic-iv-ext-cdm/1.1/
 * Used features: HPI (History of Present Illness), PE (Physical Examination), Diagnostic csv files 
